course: dictionary
lesson: 3444
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Face is one of them. The words around it tell you which meaning is right. «A cube has 6 faces» is about maths, and face means a flat side of a solid shape, not a person's face.
explain: «A family dog in Ohio ... bit her face and she needed stitches.» Here the clues are bit, stitches and she, so face means the front of a person's head. Always ask: which meaning fits the words around it? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check.
explain: Face can also be an action. «Messages ... never send what you would not say face to face» uses a phrase. Face to face means in person, with people close together. Face is a verb in other sentences, such as «face a problem», which means deal with it bravely.
fact: Face can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: Your face is the front of your head, with your eyes, nose and mouth.
fact: A face is also a flat side of a solid shape: a cube has 6 faces.
fact: A clock face is the front part with the numbers, used to tell the time.
fact: To face something means to turn toward it, or to deal with it bravely. «Face to face» means in person.
exercise: In «A cube has 6 faces», what does face mean? | To turn toward something | *A flat side of a solid shape | The front of a clock with numbers | The front of your head
exercise: In «she throws soft snowballs at nobody's face», what does face mean? | *The front of a person's head | To deal with a problem bravely | To look toward something | A flat side of a solid shape
exercise: Mia must face her fear of the dark. What does face mean here? | *To deal with something bravely | To make a funny face | A flat side of a box | The front of a clock
test: «You never send what you would not say face to face.» What does face to face mean? | Sent by post | *In person, in the same place | Shared online with a photo | Written on a card
test: Ben pulls a funny face when he tastes the lemon. What is he doing? | Looking at the clock face | Turning toward the lemon | *Twisting his face to show a feeling | Counting the flat sides of the lemon
exam: How many faces does a square pyramid have? | 8 | 4 | 6 | *5
